---
term: Electoral bundling
section: comparisons
order: 10
definition: The packaging of many unrelated decisions into a single vote for a candidate or party.
seeAlso:
  - representation-vector
  - delegation-of-functions
---
In conventional representative democracy, a voter chooses one candidate who then decides on everything from taxes to transit to foreign policy. The Social Charter unbundles these questions. Each common interest gets its own charter, objectives, and amendment process.

```diagram
Conventional

Voter
  ▼ Candidate or party
  ▼ Broad mandate
  ▼ Many unrelated decisions
```

```diagram
Social Charter

Individual
  ▼ Many interest corporations
  ▼ Specific charters and objectives
  ▼ Recursive coordination
  ▼ Delegated execution
```
